aised controversy last month, which came as no surprise to District 16 Councilmember Ginny Welsch, who has tried unsuccessfully to apply similar upzonings in the neighborhoods she represents. CM Welsch joins host Marie Cecile Anderson to talk about why she’s not giving up on the density conversation, as well as why she’s pursuing her recent request to audit Metro’s Office of Homeless Services due to financial irregularities.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGet more from City Cast Nashville when you become a \u003ca href=\"http://membership.citycast.fm/nashville\"\u003eCity Cast Nashville Neighbor\u003c/a\u003e. You’ll enjoy perks like ad-free listening, invitations to members only events and more. Join now at \u003ca href=\"http://membership.citycast.fm/nashville\"\u003emembership.citycast.fm/nashville\u003c/a\u003e  \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWant some more City Cast Nashville news? Then make sure to sign up for our\u003ca href=\"https://nashville.citycast.fm/subscribe-hey-nashville-newsletter-tennessee\"\u003e Hey Nashville newsletter. \u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFollow us\u003ca href=\"https://www.instagram.com/citycastnashville/\"\u003e @citycastnashville\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can also text us or leave a voicemail at: 615-200-6392\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eInterested in advertising with City Cast? Find more info \u003ca href=\"https://citycast.fm/advertise/\"\u003eHERE\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e","duration":"1572.21","keyphrases":["councilmember ginny welsch","cm welsch","metro office of homeless services due to financial irregularities","more from city cast nashville","city cast nashville neighbor","more city cast nashville news","nashville newsletter"],"keysentences":["The successful large-scale rezoning of the Nations raised controversy last month, which came as no surprise to District 16 Councilmember Ginny Welsch, who has tried unsuccessfully to apply similar upzonings in the neighborhoods she represents.","CM Welsch joins host Marie Cecile Anderson to talk about why she’s not giving up on the density conversation, as well as why she’s pursuing her recent request to audit Metro’s Office of Homeless Services due to financial irregularities.","Get more from City Cast Nashville when you become a City Cast Nashville Neighbor."],"keywords":["welsch","homeless","services","councilmember","office","nashville"],"path":"/podcasts/why-this-councilmember-wants-to-audit-the-office-of-homeless-services","slug":"why-this-councilmember-wants-to-audit-the-office-of-homeless-services","tags":null,"title":"Why This Councilmember Wants To Audit the Office of Homeless Services","topic":null,"uid":"CC8426781145","id":"CC8426781145","src":"https://dcs.megaphone.fm/CC8426781145.mp3","shareableUrl":"https://megaphone.link/CC8426781145","ogImageUrl":null,"image":{"_type":"image","asset":{"_ref":"image-a73f7ad19af9dac258a3b5fab539b90de5434fc6-3000x3000-png","_type":"reference"}},"author":"City Cast Nashville","metaDescription":"The successful large-scale rezoning of the Nations raised controversy last month, which came as no surprise to District 16 Councilmember Ginny Wels...","podcastEpisodes":[{"_createdAt":"2026-09-03T09:10:27Z","_id":"nashville.844428da-a712-11f1-9120-03b92d4455bc","_nlpGeneratedAt":1788426627883,"_rev":"F3oznoeAHRmzuDmXJVLHBO","_type":"podcast","_updatedAt":"2026-09-03T09:10:27Z","audioFile":"https://storage.googleapis.com/off-platform-audio-distribution/7782719543e1e55de137745d45671010d1f121f1?X-Goog-Algorithm=GOOG4-RSA-SHA256\u0026X-Goog-Credential=creator-media-transcoder%40gke-accounts.iam.gserviceaccount.com%2F20260903%2Fauto%2Fstorage%2Fgoog4_request\u0026X-Goog-Date=20260903T091025Z\u0026X-Goog-Expires=172800\u0026X-Goog-SignedHeaders=host\u0026X-Goog-","date":"2026-09-03","description":"\u003cp\u003eThis year, the \u003ca href=\"https://fristartmuseum.org/\"\u003eFrist Art Museum\u003c/a\u003e is celebrating 25 years in Nashville. Host Rachel Iacovone is joined by executive director and CEO Dr. Seth Feman to look back at the city’s changing art scene, the museum’s early years, and how the Frist has worked to make art more accessible to Nashvillians of all ages. Plus, Seth shares what he’s most excited about in the Frist’s newly announced \u003ca href=\"https://fristartmuseum.org/article/frist-art-museum-2027-schedule-of-exhibitions/\"\u003e2027 schedule of exhibitions\u003c/a\u003e and what the next 25 years could hold.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLearn more about the sponsors of this September 3rd episode:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.nashvilleballet.com/\"\u003eNashville Ballet\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.gulfshores.com/\"\u003eAlabama Beaches\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGet more from City Cast Nashville when you become a \u003ca href=\"http://membership.citycast.fm/nashville\"\u003eCity Cast Nashville Neighbor\u003c/a\u003e. You’ll enjoy perks like ad-free listening, invitations to members only events and more. Join now at\u003ca href=\"https://account.citycast.fm/become-a-neighbor/nashville?utm_source=show_notes\u0026amp;utm_medium=pod\u0026amp;utm_campaign=pod_promo\"\u003e membership.citycast.fm/nashville\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWant some more City Cast Nashville news? Then make sure to sign up for our \u003ca href=\"https://nashville.citycast.fm/subscribe-hey-nashville-newsletter-tennessee\"\u003eCity Cast Nashville newsletter.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFollow us \u003ca href=\"https://www.instagram.com/citycastnashville/\"\u003e@citycastnashville\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can also text us or leave a voicemail at: 615-200-6392\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eInterested in advertising with City Cast? Find more info \u003ca href=\"https://citycast.fm/advertise/\"\u003eHERE\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e","duration":"1377.59","keyphrases":["frist art museum","years in nashville","ceo dr. seth 